# BenchmarkDotNet writes its raw logs and per-run reports here. The deliverable is
# RFID_Throughput_Benchmark.md, which is written by hand from them.
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# The shopper token signing key, generated on first run where none is configured, and the database
# backups. Both are per-host state that lives inside the application folder because that is the one
# place an IIS pool identity can reliably write. Committing either would publish a credential or a
# copy of the shop's data.
App_Data/

# LaTeX build detritus
docs/software-stack/*.log
docs/software-stack/*.aux
docs/software-stack/*.toc
docs/software-stack/*.lof
docs/software-stack/*.lot
docs/software-stack/*.out

# Files that have been sitting loose in the working tree, named here before somebody
# types `git add -A` into a public repository.
#
# SignUpCredientials.txt is one line holding the live administrator's e-mail and
# password in clear text. It is ignored rather than tidied away because deleting it
# does not help: the next person to write it down recreates it under the same name.
# The password itself still has to be changed -- an ignore rule stops it being
# published, it does not unpublish anything.
SignUpCredientials.txt
*Credientials*.txt
*Credentials*.txt

# Packaged agent builds. Thirty-five megabytes of compiled output that the deploy
# pipeline does not consume -- the terminal agent is installed on a till by hand -- so
# committing them bloats every clone for no gain.
retail25-agent.zip
till-installer-kit.zip

# Runtime output from a local API run, and the file that parks the site during a
# deploy. Both are per-run state, not source.
api-run.log
api-stdout.log
api-stderr.log
app_offline.htm
